spec gg03-degree-and-count-at-snapshot: 2 sessions, 21 permutations
# GG03. s0 pins a read snapshot and reads the hub's degree and the :R relationship
# count — the count-store answer (seek) beside a typed scan (scan) — twice; s1 adds an
# edge into the hub and deletes one in two autocommit statements. s0's repeated reads
# are equal, and seek = scan in every read.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s0d1 s0r1 s0d2 s0r2 s0c s1a s1d
step s0d1: MATCH (h:N {name:'hub'}) OPTIONAL MATCH (h)--(m) RETURN count(m) AS degree
degree
------
3     
(1 row)
